Subject: Cantor Scribe Semantic Kernel P0 Justification

@ [justification_uuid] 85432b68-5753-4e07-9485-ae01a40cbe65
@ [specification_uuid] b09b4613-000b-4621-89de-6d81ef64f7f3

& [Problem]
  + Cantor can host SOP Eclipse structurally but its published base does not yet own the mature semantic interpretation nucleus developed in the live instance checkout
  + cantor_scribe mixes that reusable nucleus with storage project I/O query revision LSP MCP Tokio and provider-facing service surfaces
  + admitting the whole crate would collapse kernel component instance and effect boundaries

& [Decision]
  + extract only reviewed in-memory forms normalization digests validation expression evaluation and source analysis into cantor_sop_semantics
  + preserve exact upstream byte identities and carry transformation attribution into evidence
  + replace ambient and database fault conversions with a bounded semantic fault
  + require stricter supplied machine forms than the observed candidate where semantic sets otherwise erase duplicates

& [WhyNow]
  + the published instance foundation explicitly holds cantor_scribe for separate promotion
  + semantic analysis is the highest-leverage provider-free substrate needed by SOP Eclipse and later Cantor instances
  + doing this before more instance-only work reduces divergence and gives future components a stable meaning boundary

& [Rejected]
  + no wholesale copy or implicit acceptance of the live crate
  + no SQLite filesystem project discovery LSP MCP Tokio provider model or remote capability
  + no mutation cleanup staging or normalization of the live C checkout
  + no inference that historical Eclipse tests satisfy current Cantor workspace gates
